Z||000000||86SE||02-09-2000||10:02 PM||||Has anyone wire lights (maybe christmas lights) in their car to blink with the bass in their stereo system??<P>I heard of someone doing this and wondered how hard it would be....I'm thinking you would have to wire them in the path to your sub, or on the output terminals on your amp, but my amp puts out 500-800 watts to my sub, would that burn out the little bulbs??<P>That would be really cool to have!!!||||reg||3
Z||000001||TOM||02-09-2000||11:56 PM||||go to radio shack and get the little box kit thing that controls the light from the sound of the music not the current path. Besides thats watts not amps/volts on your output.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-10-2000||08:14 AM||||just curious.. what size cable are you using to power and ground said amp? and what amp fuse are you using? Not related to the light question just wondering...||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||02-10-2000||08:43 AM||||power and ground wire is 4 guage, there are 2 25amp fuses on the amp and 1 huge fuse on the power power wire. (35 amp maybe)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||02-10-2000||04:02 PM||||4 gauge......thats a tad overboard even for an 800 watt amp||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||02-10-2000||04:27 PM||||I think if you just drive with stereo thumping and turn on your dome lights it would do the same, no mods.  Just kidding, kind of.  It wouldn’t be hard to do.  I’ve seen a  black ball about the size of a softball the had different colored lenses in it and a light would move back and forth inside the ball. Tadaaaaa, beams of light.  Think it came from like  Spencer Gifts. A lot of the cheap home lighting effect systems use  low voltage.  Just check the ac adapters and  see if they are around 12 volts. And most of them work off of sound.||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||02-10-2000||05:12 PM||||there are people driving around with 1 guage power wire to amps that have a max output of 1000 watts......................................||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gokart||02-10-2000||07:47 PM||||Have a buddy that drives a Isuzu Impulse and he has long blue lights mounted under each rocker panel and has it rigged so they flicker with the bass! Flickering lights with bass is kind of a "ricey" thing if you ask me. Just my 2cents!||||reg||2
